"answer": "Project Zenith is a new data analytics initiative launched with a kick-off on June 15th, led by Sarah Tan, and initially budgeted at $500,000 for phase one. The project team was expanded in September with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture. Key milestones include the successful completion of the testing phase and the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype, which was celebrated in October. Phase two has achieved a breakthrough in predictive analytics, with a detailed report scheduled for the November 20th staff meeting. Stakeholder feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is being sought by the end of November. Additionally, the compliance plan's budget was increased to $55,000, and security protocols, including multi-factor authentication and encryption at rest, are set to be updated effective January next year."
